# The promoted champion is a build artifact of the training pipeline, not source.
# The promoted champion is COMMITTED, and that is a deploy-target decision.
#
# Vercel builds from git and has no model registry to fetch from, so an ignored
# artifact means the deployed app serves its honest "no model deployed" 503 to
# every visitor -- a failure that looks like a working page. At 2,427 bytes the
# usual argument against binaries in git does not apply.
#
# The container path still prefers the registry: azure/ml/fetch_model.py
# overwrites these before `docker build`, and re-checks the promotion gates
# against the checked-out extractor while doing it. Git is the floor; the
# registry is the authority when there is one. See D-030 and D-032.
# (Deliberately NOT ignored: model/champion.onnx, model/champion.meta.json)
